SUMMARY:20s & 30s Trail Work Weekend - Camp Dodge
LOCATION:1 Camp Dodge R\nGorham\, NH 03581
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 2\, 2026 | 4:00 PM\nhttps://activities.outdoo
 rs.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001GWZd2AO/\nShovels and mattocks and axes\, 
 oh my! Do you hear the call? It's trail work time! Your fellow 20s & 30s a
 re ready to get down and dirty\, are you ready to join?Two nights and two 
 days at the Camp Dodge Trails Center in Gorham\, NH\, in the heart of the 
 White Mountains. Under the instruction of staff from the AMC Trails Depart
 ment we'll lend our time and hands to bolstering the good work done by AMC
  Pro Crews all over the region. In years past we've installed bog bridges\
 , done rock work\, installed boardwalks\, and more! The work is vigorous b
 ut good for the soul and amazing to see results that will pay off for deca
 des to come.This trip includes 2 nights (Friday and Saturday) stay in one 
 of the shared bunkhouses at Camp Dodge (we'll have one to our group\, but 
 we will be sharing) and delicious dinner Friday and Saturday + breakfast &
  lunch Saturday and Sunday (dietary needs will be met). Each day we'll ral
 ly after breakfast\, go through the plan for the day\, load ourselves and 
 our gear up\, and then off to the worksite. We'll put in a full day on Sat
 urday and a partial day on Sunday so we all have a chance to head home.Thi
 s trip is intended for people in their 20s & 30s with an interest in trail
  work\, conservation\, and preserving the outdoors we know and love. No tr
 ail work experience is required\, but is always welcome! All you need is a
  desire to learn and the ability to meet a minimum physical threshold. Wor
 k each day will involve hiking a few miles while carrying your pack\, tool
 s\, and any necessary supplies over varied terrain with a moderate elevati
 on gain. It's good work but it can be hard work. Prepare to be sore and ti
 red but filled with the warm glow of knowing your contributions matter!At 
 the end of our work days\, we'll be relaxing and socializing around Camp D
 odge. There's nothing like a day digging in the dirt to make fast friends 
 with your fellow crewmates!This trip costs $50. Your fee goes directly to 
 the cost of food at the Camp Dodge kitchen.If you have any questions at al
 l\, please let your leaders know! We're happy to provide more information 
 and to hopefully see you out there!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX000001JVlt2AG
