SUMMARY:20s & 30s Apple Picking at Berlin Orchards
LOCATION:310 Sawyer Hill R\nBerlin\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 10\, 2026\nhttps://activities.outdoors.org/
 s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001JdTJ2A0/\nJoin us for a quintessential New Englan
 d fall pastime -- apple picking at Berlin Orchards in Central Mass! We'll 
 ride the hay wagon to the fields and pick classic varieties\, including Jo
 nagold\, Honey Crisp\, Golden Supreme\, Cortland\, Gala\, Paula Red and Ma
 cintosh.Afterwards\, enjoy cider donuts\, apple cider\, and kettle corn\, 
 compliments of the Worcester Chapter! Check out the farm store for pumpkin
 s\, squash\, seasonal favorites\, and local honey.We are a group within AM
 C that is dedicated to encouraging people in their 20s and 30s to enjoy th
 e outdoors. Meet like-minded outdoor enthusiasts and enjoy a fun and relax
 ing time at the orchard. We request folks to register so that we can get a
  count of participants and get in touch if anything changes. Space is limi
 ted. This event is in partnership with the Worcester Chapter Social Commit
 tee.Please no dogs as they are not allowed in the orchard due to sanitary 
 and safety reasons. Note: start and end times are approximate and details 
 will be sent to registered participants.Note: The orchard charges admissio
 n in the form of apple picking bags. Here's the breakdown:$40 - 1/2 bushel
  bag (holds ~20 lbs worth of apples\, admits 5 people to orchard)$30 - 1 p
 eck (holds ~10 lbs worth of apples\, admits 3 people to orchard) Particip
 ants can feel free to split the cost of bags with fellow participants (tip
 : bring cash if you plan to do so)\; arrangements can be made at the event
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX000001KJyn2AG
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261004T042552Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:20s & 30s Dayhike to Royalston Falls and Socializing at Red Apple 
 Farms
LOCATION:362 Athol-Richmond R\nRoyalston\, MA 01368
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, October 11\, 2026\nhttps://activities.outdoors.org/s/
 oc-activity/a5UVX000001KJyn2AG/\nJoin us on a hike to one of Massachusetts
 ’ most stunning waterfalls\, followed by some apple picking and socializ
 ing at Red Apple Farm.We will start with an out-and-back hike to Royalston
  Falls\, covering about 2 miles with a total elevation gain of 300 ft. We 
 will then head to Red Apple Farm to pick apples\, grab food\, and enjoy so
 me live music.The trail will include sections of moderate terrain and we w
 ill be moving at a moderate pace. In particular\, there are some steep sec
 tions that may have wet\, slippery leaves. Proper equipment will be requir
 ed for this hike\, including hiking and weather appropriate clothing and w
 ater. No dogs please. We are a group within AMC that is dedicated to enco
 uraging people in their 20s and 30s to enjoy the outdoors.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX000001Jjgn2AC
