DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:20's & 30's Interchapter Fall Fest: Almuerzo con los 20's & 30's -
  Cooking Brunch at Douglas State Forest
LOCATION:Douglas\, MA 01516
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 17\, 2026 | 10:00 AM\nhttps://activities.ou
 tdoors.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001Jjgn2AC/\nJoin the Worcester 20's & 30
 's for an outdoor cooking lesson and short hike at Douglas State Forest!Sa
 l Vazquez Reyes will teach the group how to make sopes\, a tradition Mexic
 an dish made with corn masa and beans. For the toppings\, we will make a c
 actus salad and salsa. For drinks\, we can make a refreshing Jamaica agua 
 fresca. After cooking\, we will have a nice brunch all together. During th
 e instruction\, attendees will work in small groups at cooking stations\, 
 with use of a charcoal grill.After brunch\, we will have the option to do 
 a short hike at Douglas State Forest. The exact length and route of this h
 ike will depend on participant interest\, and how much time is leftover be
 fore the full Interchapter Social at Treehouse Brewing at 4pm (more detail
 s on that below). Also\, for this hike afterward\, it is requested that pa
 rticpants wear something of a blaze orange color\, as it is hunting season
 . Please reach out to Luke if you don't have any of these items.As time ge
 ts closer\, participants will be sent out an excel sheet to sign up for wh
 at cooking equipment they can bring. Please plan to bring at least a coupl
 e of these items to ensure we have enough for each group. These items incl
 ude cooking pan\, cutting board\, knife\, saucepan\, tongs\, wooden spoons
 \, and bowls. The leaders will bring all of the food needed for cooking\, 
 and there will be a cost of $12 per participant to help cover this. Detail
 s for this payment will be sent after registration. Registration is requir
 ed for attendance\, and registration closes on Tuesday 10/13 at 8pm to all
 ow for us to prepare accordingly. Hope to have you join us!This event is p
 art of the 20's & 30's Interchapter Fall Fest: Social at Tree House Brewin
 g Company in Charlton\, MA with the Connecticut\, Narragansett\, Southeast
 ern MA\, Western MA\, and Worcester MA chapters. After the hike\, particip
 ants are encouraged to attend the Social at Treehouse Brewing in Charlton\
 , MA at 4pm. Please register for the Tree House Social at this link: https
 ://activities.outdoors.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001Id8o/act00023773.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX000001K5m92AC
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261004T042552Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:20's & 30's Interchapter Fall Fest: Wells State Park
LOCATION:Wells State Park\, 159 Walker Pond R\nSturbridge\, MA 01566
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 17\, 2026 | 11:45 AM\nhttps://activities.ou
 tdoors.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001K5m92AC/\nCelebrate fall and join us f
 or a 6 mile hike through the scenic forests of Wells State Park. The trail
 s will offer easy to moderate terrain with a total elevation gain of 500-f
 t and we plan to move at a moderate pace between 1.5 and 2 mph.Proper equi
 pment will be required for this hike\, including: hiking and weather appro
 priate clothing\, water\, a day pack\, trail snacks\, and raingear. No dog
 s please. As hunting season has begun\, it is advisable to wear blaze ora
 nge (vest or hat) while hiking.After the hike\, you are invited to join us
  at a nearby (15 minutes away) social with other 20's and 30's from the Na
 rragansett\, Worcester\, Western MA\, Connecticut\, and Southeast Massachu
 setts AMC chapters.If you are interested\, please register for the Tree Ho
 use Social at this link: https://activities.outdoors.org/s/oc-activity/a5U
 VX000001Id8o/act00023773.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX000001JOcL2AW
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261004T042552Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:20s & 30s Squam Traverse
LOCATION:Sandwich Notch Road\nSandwich\, NH
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, October 25\, 2026\nhttps://activities.outdoors.org/s/
 oc-activity/a5UVX000001JOcL2AW/\nJoin the Worcester 20s & 30s group for a 
 hike in the Squam Lake region on Sunday\, October 25th! We will hike the S
 quam Traverse\, an approximately 12-mile hike along the Crawford-Ridgepole
  trail. We'll summit four peaks and enjoy views from this trail along the 
 Squam Range.This hike will have approx. 2\,850 ft of elevation gain. Our i
 ntention is to go at a roughly 1.5 mile per hour pace. Expect to be on tra
 il for the full day.We intend to summit Mts Percival and Morgan\, which ar
 e both "52 With a View" hikes. This will be a one-way hike with a car spot
 . We may ask some participants to help with driving members of our group b
 etween the trailheads.Sturdy shoes with laces\, at least 2 liters of water
 \, nutritious snacks/lunch\, and appropriate layers of clothing are requir
 ed. Participants should be prepared for numerous steep ups and downs and l
 edgy and rough terrain in sections.No dogs\, please. Further details\, suc
 h as start time and location\, will be provided to participants after they
  complete the required screening form\, which will be sent after registeri
 ng. Hope to have you join us!
END:VEVENT
